[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/136861027","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409#issuecomment-136861027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409","id":136861027,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNjg2MTAyNw==","user":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-01T21:04:14Z","updated_at":"2015-09-01T21:04:14Z","body":"We should certainly get rid of the ugly error.  That they aren't duplicate symbols is an interesting idea, I'm not sure whether that would be confusing or convenient.\n\n> Other options include ensuring rules like groovy.bzl use uniquish names such as @junit-groovy, but this leads to annoying artifact duplication. A better solution might be for groovy.bzl to rely on //external targets, which would give users some flexibility in how they're bound. I'm happy to make these changes to the groovy rules.\n\ngroovy.bzl should rely on //external targets for exactly the reasons you mention.  We'd be happy to accept patches for that.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reacti