orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"assigned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-09-01T21:04:18Z","assignee":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/136968927","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409#issuecomment-136968927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409","id":136968927,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNjk2ODkyNw==","user":{"login":"ekuefler","id":666477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/666477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler","html_url":"https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-02T07:57:22Z","updated_at":"2015-09-02T07:57:22Z","body":"I sent https://bazel-review.googlesource.com/#/c/1940/ to do the groovy rules.\n\nWith my current approach to workspaces I think it would be convenient if I could re-use names between artifacts and bindings, but I'm not certain my current approach is the best one, and I keep making tweaks to how I do it. It might be useful for the Bazel team to provide more documentation/guidance around best practices here. My current approach has the following properties:\n- Every external dependency is defined via a `bind` rule in WORKSPACE. Normal code only ever references these bindings via the `external` package, it never refers directly to `@` targets.\n- External artifacts (`maven_jar`, `http_repository`, etc.) are all named like `mydep-raw`. In the simple case where the artifact has no transitive deps, it's bound as `bind(name = \"mydep\", actual = \"@mydep-raw//jar\")` or similar.\n- For artifacts with transitive dependencies, I have a top-level BUILD file that defines `java_libraries` containing only `exports` and `runtime_deps`. These are the only libraries allowed to refer to to `@` raw targets, which go in either `exports` or `runtime_deps` depending on whether the artifact defines the library's API or it's a transitive dependency.\n\nThis is working okay but there are still a few things I don't like about it:\n- `-raw` suffix required on all the artifacts is annoying and feels unnecessary (the part this bug is about).\n- Have to split the definition of a single library across three places (the binding in WORKSPACE, artifacts in WORKSPACE, and then the dependency declarations in a BUILD). It feels like I should be able to configure the transitive deps right in WORKSPACE.\n- Transitive dep warnings instruct developers to add the raw `@` targets to their BUILD files, which have to be mapped back to external bindings manually.\n- The `java_libraries` used to define the deps mean I wind up with a bunch of empty jars in the top level of bazel-bin/\n\nI kind of drifted from the scope of this bug there, but hopefully it's useful for understanding how I'm currently interacting with bindings and external artifacts.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/136968927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ekuefler","id":666477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/666477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler","html_url":"https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":399058695,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDM5OTA1ODY5NQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/399058695","actor":{"login":"fweikert","id":12609729,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjA5NzI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12609729?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert","html_url":"https://github.com/fweikert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fweikert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"0ec12165ee8406b4b6382b5779f50e73d8a2693e","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/commits/0ec12165ee8406b4b6382b5779f50e73d8a2693e","created_at":"2015-09-02T15:15:27Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/137760247","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409#issuecomment-137760247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409","id":137760247,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNzc2MDI0Nw==","user":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-04T15:02:30Z","updated_at":"2015-09-04T15:02:30Z","body":"Thanks for the groovy patch!\n\n> Have to split the definition of a single library across three places (the binding in WORKSPACE, artifacts in WORKSPACE, and then the dependency declarations in a BUILD). It feels like I should be able to configure the transitive deps right in WORKSPACE.\n\nI was thinking that it would be good to add deps (and runtime_deps) fields to the maven_jar rule.  That might alleviate some of this pain. It's less obvious to me how other scope should be handled. \n\nThis also would also take care of the empty jars at top level.\n\n> Transitive dep warnings instruct developers to add the raw @ targets to their BUILD files, which have to be mapped back to external bindings manually.\n\nNot sure if it'd help, but you don't have to bind all of the maven_jars, if you don't want to.  It makes your code a bit less portable (users might not be able to import it as an external repository), but if it's not an open source library, you should be okay.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/137760247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/138816522","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409#issuecomment-138816522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/409","id":138816522,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzODgxNjUyMg==","user":{"login":"ekuefler","id":666477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/666477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler","html_url":"https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-09T07:55:13Z","updated_at":"2015-09-09T07:55:13Z","body":"> I was thinking that it would be good to add deps (and runtime_deps) fields to the maven_jar rule. That might alleviate some of this pain.\n\n+1, that would be excellent. I'd think `http_jar` would need it also.\n\n> Not sure if it'd help, but you don't have to bind all of the maven_jars, if you don't want to. It makes your code a bit less portable (users might not be able to import it as an external repository), but if it's not an open source library, you should be okay.\n\nFor the time being I want to avoid the inconsistency of using `//external` for targets with transitive deps and `@` for targets without them. But if the artifact rules supported dependencies this would become a much less compelling argument.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/138816522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ekuefler","id":666477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/666477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler","html_url":"https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use